 passing bills to significantly  restrict voting in ways that would  disproportionately  hurt communities of color just this year  state lawmakers have already issued at  least 389 restrictive bills in 49 states  and passed  22 restrictive laws in 14 states  it's no coincidence that the four states  where republicans have filed the most  bills aimed at restricting voting  georgia arizona michigan and  pennsylvania  were some of the closest states in the  2020 presidential election as 5  38 notes all four of those states went  for biden and have republican-controlled  legislatures which makes them especially  ripe for new voting restrictions so  three reasons here really why you are  seeing this republican opposition  one the commission would likely find  that  they were part of the problem two they  want to stay in donald trump's good  graces because it seems trump is going  to have power and control in the  republican party for a long period of  time to come at least through the 2022  election  if he fails to pick the winners in 2022  things may change but at least through  2022 and number three  if they can continue uh putting off  a real investigation into what happened  which would of course  uncover that the election was fine the  election wasn't rigged  joe biden just won they  lose the ability if that is made public  through the commission  to keep justifying these further  restrictions on voting  that they're passing in many states so  democrats  need to move forward with the probe  without any republicans there's a couple  of ways that it could happen  it would then actually be a partisan  commission now i know what you might be  thinking  you know david republicans falsely say  we don't want to participate in this  because it's going to be partisan  and then as a result democrats just move  forward and it is partisan  that is that that is of course what they  are going to claim  but the benefits of doing the commission  by far outweigh  claims from republi